<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan eases rules on gold jewellery exports.</title>
<headline>Pakistan eases rules on gold jewellery exports.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan on Saturday eased restrictions on exports of gold jewellery, an SBP official said.</p>
<p>He said that indigenous precious and semi-precious stones and gold jewellery could now be exported without central bank approval. An exporter would need only certification from an authorised foreign exchange dealer as evidence of realisation of export proceeds, he added.</p>
</text>
